Bootstrap: docker
From: python:3.12-slim

%help
    TPC solver (CP-SAT) image, Python 3.12, CPU-only, lightweight deps.

    Build (requires root OR --fakeroot OR a Sylabs --remote token):
        module load singularity/4.4
        singularity build tpc-solver-py312.sif slurm/tpc-solver-py312.def

    On clusters with no fakeroot/remote/proot (e.g. this BeeGFS cluster, where
    we have no subuid/subgid allocation), a %post cannot run as non-root. Use the
    rootless equivalent slurm/build_image.sh instead (base python:3.12-slim SIF
    + bind-mounted 3.12 venv with the SAME pinned deps). Keep the two pin lists
    in sync.

%labels
    Maintainer fabimi
    Project china-travel-agent
    Purpose Lightweight TPC solver (CP-SAT) image for Slurm compute nodes
    Python 3.12
    Notes |
        Matches .python-version (3.12) and the project's 3.12-only convention.
        Contains ONLY the non-optional deps of the TPCAgent/TPCLLM import chain.
        Heavy deps (torch/vllm/transformers/flashinfer/modelscope/openai) are
        optional in chinatravel/agent/llms.py (try/except -> None) and are
        intentionally OMITTED to keep the image small and CPU-only. Add a CUDA
        base + --nv for any future real-LLM work.
        Pinned to the exact versions the repo builds with for reproducibility.
        Build note: %post needs root/fakeroot; see slurm/build_image.sh for the
        rootless (base-sif + bind-venv) path used on this cluster.

%post
    # pip up to date, no cache to shrink layers
    pip install --no-cache-dir --upgrade pip
    pip install --no-cache-dir \
      numpy==2.4.6 \
      pandas==2.2.3 \
      geopy==2.4.1 \
      fuzzywuzzy==0.18.0 \
      python-Levenshtein==0.27.1 \
      scikit-learn==1.5.2 \
      tqdm==4.66.6 \
      func-timeout==4.3.5 \
      datasets==3.3.2 \
      ortools==9.15.6755 \
      z3-solver==4.14.1.0 \
      jsonschema==4.23.0 \
      json-repair==0.30.0 \
      packaging==24.2

%test
    # Build-time self-check: every solver import must resolve.
    python -c "import ortools,z3,numpy,pandas,sklearn,geopy,func_timeout,datasets,json_repair,jsonschema,fuzzywuzzy; print('import-ok')"

%runscript
    exec python "$@"
